 "summary": "The creator shares a personal experience where a newly hired video editor accused him of being bossy and arrogant, wanting to complain to the boss. This incident made the creator realize that he had failed to establish his managerial authority, teaching him that people cannot respect your humility or understand your capability if you hide your achievements.",
 "key_points": [
  "The creator recently hired a video editor who accused him of being bossy and arrogant after just three days and wanted to complain to the boss.",
  "The creator's perspective changed when he realized that the new editor never saw him as a manager, but rather as a colleague trying to exercise authority.",
  "The creator claims he was so focused on being humble that he forgot that people cannot understand your humility if they do not know your capability.",
  "The creator points out that you call someone humble when you know they are successful and have achieved something yet behave like an ordinary person.",
  "The creator warns that hiding what you have achieved or what you are capable of just to avoid sounding arrogant means people might never understand what you bring to the table or respect your word."
 ],
 "content": "Instagram reel/post by Abhiram. Text / caption: I’m not asking you to boast about yourself obviously, but do not under value yourselves either. Transcript: Stop being too humble! So we recently hired a video editor and three days in, he accused me of being bossy and arrogant and he wanted to meet my boss to complain about me. I was like what the hell when did I even behave with this guy like that? Because from my perspective, I was trying to guide him, give him feedback and push him to learn more. But while sitting in front of my boss and listening to his side of the story, he said something that completely changed my perspective. I thought you were just another video editor like me. I never even realized you are a manager until now. And it hit me in that exact moment. In those three days, he never even saw me as a manager. I became a colleague who's trying to exercise authority on him and it taught me a very important flaw in my leadership. I was so focused on being humble all the time that I forgot to realize, how can someone understand your humility if they don't know your capability? Think about it. You call someone down to earth or humble when you know they are successful and have achieved something yet behave like an ordinary person. If you hide what you've achieved or what you're capable of just because you might sound arrogant, people might never understand what you bring to the table and they might never respect your word. One realization changed the way I communicate to people. That's the story for this week. Follow along if you want to see what an ambitious 20-year-old is doing with his life. On screen text: Stop being too humble!, VIDEO EDITOR AND THREE DAYS IN, HE ACCUSED ME, BOSSY AND ARROGANT AND, Actual messages, WITH THIS GUY LIKE THAT?, BECAUSE FROM MY PERSPECTIVE, TRYING TO GUIDE HIM, GIVE HIM FEEDBACK, AND PUSH HIM TO LEARN MORE, BUT WHILE SITTING IN, FRONT OF MY BOSS AND, LISTENING TO HIS SIDE OF THE, STORY, THAT COMPLETELY CHANGED, MY PERSPECTIVE, ANOTHER VIDEO EDITOR, I NEVER EVEN REALIZED, YOU ARE A MANAGER UNTIL NOW, AND IT HIT ME IN THAT, EXACT MOMENT, IN THOSE THREE DAYS, HE, NEVER EVEN SAW ME, I BECAME A COLLEAGUE, WHO'S TRYING TO EXERCISE, AUTHORITY ON HIM, AND IT, TAUGHT ME A VERY IMPORTANT, ME A VERY IMPORTANT, IN MY LEADERSHIP, ASSUME THAT ME, I WAS SO FOCUSED ON, TIME THAT I FORGOT TO, CAN SOMEONE UNDERSTAND, YOUR HUMILITY IF THEY, DON'T KNOW YOUR, CAPABILITY, YOU CALL SOMEONE DOWN TO, EARTH OR HUMBLE WHEN YOU, KNOW THEY ARE SUCCESSFUL, AND HAVE ACHIEVED, SOMETHING YET BEHAVE, LIKE AN ORDINARY PERSON, IF YOU HIDE WHAT YOU'VE, ACHIEVED OR WHAT YOU'RE, CAPABLE OF JUST BECAUSE, YOU MIGHT SOUND ARROGANT, PEOPLE MIGHT NEVER, UNDERSTAND WHAT YOU, BRING TO THE, TABLE AND THEY MIGHT, NEVER RESPECT YOUR WORD, ONE REALIZATION CHANGED, THE WAY I COMMUNICATE TO, THAT'S THE STORY FOR, THIS WEEK, FOLLOW ALONG IF YOU WANT, TO SEE WHAT AN AMBITIOUS, 20-YEAR-OLD IS DOING, WITH HIS LIFE",
